Found by the B052 lane, 2026-08-30, via live RemoteBuild probe of 1639
qualified spellings against Trackmania + Openplanet 1.29.5. Deliberately kept
OUT of B052, which is scoped to the `has_enum` tail fallback.

## Defect
On the same 1639 spellings, the merge-base LSP reports **zero** errors while
the game rejects **1010**. These are false NEGATIVES: the LSP stays silent on
code that will not compile.

Two distinct causes, neither of which is the tail fallback:

**(a) Exact-key acceptance of the synthetic module prefix.** The Nadeo loader
keys types as `Module::Class` / `Module::Class::Enum`. Those module prefixes
are the LSP's own invention — they exist nowhere in the game. So the index
accepts `Game::CGameCtnApp` and `Game::CGameMenu::EMenuOrder` by exact key
match, while the game answers `Namespace 'Game' doesn't exist.`

**(b) `resolve_unqualified` rescues bare nested enum names.** A bare
`EMenuOrder` resolves in the LSP; the game rejects it. Note the rescue is
CORRECT for classes and wrong only for nested ENUMS — do not remove it
wholesale.

## The rule the game actually follows
Established by the same probe (1639 spellings plus 120 paired namespace
probes). AngelScript resolves `P::T` by walking P's ancestor scopes to global:

- P is not a scope -> `Namespace 'P' doesn't exist.` (REJECT)
- P is a scope but T is not found -> `Identifier 'T' is not a data type in
  namespace 'P' or parent`
- P is a scope and T is a GLOBAL enum -> ACCEPT

And the discriminator for engine classes, 8/8 confirmed: **an engine class is
a namespace iff it declares at least one enum** (named or anonymous). Hence
`CGameMenu::VirtualKey` ACCEPT but `CSceneVehicleVis::VirtualKey` REJECT.

## Probe hygiene — applies to EVERY lane using the live game
**Namespaces from other installed plugins leak into the compile.**
`MLFeed::VirtualKey` and `VehicleState::VirtualKey` resolve on this machine
only because MLFeedRaceData.op and vehicle-state-list-dev are installed.

So the two directions are NOT symmetric:
- a game **REJECT** is solid evidence about the engine
- a game **ACCEPT** on an unknown prefix is NOT automatically an engine fact

Two anomalies (`MathX`, `GameData`) were traced to this and excluded from the
model. Any future probe must apply the same asymmetry, or it will encode the
prober's local plugin set as engine behaviour.

## Work
- Take the B052 lane's saved per-name game verdict table as the starting
  corpus rather than re-probing 1639 names. Ask that lane for it; it must be
  committed to the repo at a durable path, not left in /tmp (which filled to
  100% during this session and killed a command mid-write).
- Fix (a) by refusing the synthetic module prefix as a qualifier, keeping it
  as an internal key only.
- Fix (b) by narrowing `resolve_unqualified` for nested enums specifically,
  leaving the class behaviour intact.
- Re-verify against the game after implementing; do not assume the model
  generalises beyond the probed corpus.

## Gate
This will RAISE fixture ERROR counts substantially — that is the fix working,
and it is exactly why this is a separate ticket from B052. Every new error
must be justified by name against a recorded game REJECT from the verdict
table. An unexplained new error is a bug, not a baseline update. Measure two
binaries on the same machine at the same time (baselines at filing: 14/1485,
5/276, 2/35, 4/2, 4/4, showcase-diags 9/7 — re-measure, since B052 lands
first and may move them).

